---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import BaseHead from "../components/BaseHead.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import { AUTHOR } from "../consts";
import brianPhoto from "../assets/images/brian.jpg";
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <BaseHead
      title="About"
      description="Background, work, and how I think about engineering."
    />
  </head>
  <body>
    <Header />
    <main>
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <div class="header">
        <div class="header-text">
          <h1>How I think about engineering.</h1>
          <p class="lede">
            I build and operate production systems for organisations where
            reliability is non-negotiable — healthcare AI platforms, financial
            services, and critical infrastructure. My work sits at the
            intersection of platform engineering, cloud architecture, and
            operational excellence, translating technical decisions into
            business outcomes: uptime, resilience, regulatory confidence, and
            customer trust.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="header-photo">
          <Image
            src={brianPhoto}
            alt="Brian Muli Muteti"
            width={220}
            height={220}
            loading="eager"
          />
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>Current</h2>
      <p>
        I am currently Lead Site Reliability Engineer for Africa (Kenya Focus)
        at <strong>Qure.ai</strong>
        where I help operate, deploy and scale the ML systems that power AI-assisted
        healthcare diagnostics across multiple countries.
      </p>

      <p>
        My work spans reliability engineering, cloud infrastructure,
        observability, automation, security, platform operations, and
        operational excellence. I work closely with engineering and product
        teams to ensure critical healthcare systems remain resilient,
        observable, and scalable as adoption grows.
      </p>

      <h2>Background</h2>
      <p>
        Before joining <strong>Qure.ai</strong>, I worked as a DevOps and Site
        Reliability Engineer within one of East Africa's largest financial
        institutions, supporting mission-critical banking and payments
        platforms. Much of the work documented in my <a href="/work"
          >case studies</a
        > comes from that period.
      </p>
      <p>
        Over the course of my career, I have worked across cloud architecture,
        platform engineering, observability, incident response, automation, and
        large-scale system modernisation. I am particularly interested in
        building systems that remain simple to operate even as they grow in
        complexity.
      </p>
      <p>
        I hold a BSc in Electrical and Electronics Engineering from the
        Technical University of Mombasa, and I am a registered Graduate Engineer
        with the Engineering Board of Kenya.
      </p>

      <h2>How I work</h2>
      <p>
        I view reliability as a business outcome rather than a technical metric.
        The systems I build are observable, fault-tolerant, and designed for the
        engineers who operate them—not just the engineers who build them.
      </p>
      <p>
        I place a strong emphasis on automation, documentation, operational
        readiness, and post-incident learning. Whether responding to a
        production incident, designing a platform, or leading a migration, my
        goal is the same: leave the system and the team in a better state than I
        found them.
      </p>
      <p>
        I believe engineering leadership is earned through ownership, clear
        communication, and consistency during high-pressure situations.
      </p>

      <h2>Beyond Engineering</h2>

      <p>
        Outside of my full-time role, I have served as Head of Operations for
        the Association of Energy Professionals in Eastern Africa (AEPEA) for
        over two years, where I supported operational initiatives, technology
        programmes, and organisational growth.
      </p>

      <h2>Certifications</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>AWS Certified DevOps Engineer – Professional (DOP-C02)</li>
        <li>AWS Certified Solutions Architect – Associate (SAA-C03)</li>
        <li>AWS Cloud Quest: Generative AI Architect</li>
        <li>AWS Cloud Quest: Solutions Architect</li>
        <li>AWS Cloud Quest: Cloud Practitioner</li>
        <li>AWS Cloud Quest: Amazon Connect Fundamentals</li>
        <li>Google Data Analytics Professional Certificate</li>
        <li>Google Project Management Professional Certificate</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Get in touch</h2>
      <p>
        The best way to reach me is by <a href={`mailto:${AUTHOR.email}`}
          >email</a
        >. I am also active on <a href={AUTHOR.linkedin}>LinkedIn</a> and occasionally
        write on <a href={AUTHOR.medium}>Medium</a> about cloud engineering, reliability,
        platform operations, and emerging technologies.
      </p>
    </main>
    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  .header {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
    gap: var(--space-8);
    align-items: start;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }
  .header-text {
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .header-photo :global(img) {
    width: 180px;
    height: 180px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    object-fit: cover;
    filter: grayscale(0.1);
    display: block;
  }
  .lede {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .header {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: var(--space-6);
    }
    .header-photo {
      order: -1;
    }
    .header-photo :global(img) {
      width: 140px;
      height: 140px;
    }
  }
</style>
